# Build context exclusions for the FOUR images whose context is the repo root:
# api-gateway, backend-orchestrator, backend-temporal-adapter and
# shared/mcp-connectors/internal/kafka-mcp-sink. (Census, not memory:
# `context: .` appears at docker-compose.yml:457, :1001, :1179, :1428 and at
# .github/workflows/docker-publish.yml:61, :66, :71, :139 -- those eight sites
# are the same four Dockerfiles.)
#
# Docker reads .dockerignore ONLY from the context root. The three nested ones
# the repo already had -- frontend/, shared/mcp-connectors/ and
# connector-deployer/ -- therefore do nothing for a root-context build, and
# without this file the context those four builds ship is the WHOLE checkout.
#
# Measured on a developer machine, same checkout, same command:
#
#   without this file   context = the whole 2.7 GB tree
#                       (frontend/.next 1.7 GB + frontend/node_modules 819 MB)
#   with this file      21.09 MB transferred in 0.2 s, 46 MB materialised
#
# The `ls` of that materialised context still shows api-gateway,
# backend-orchestrator, backend-temporal-adapter and shared -- every directory
# the four Dockerfiles name -- and no longer shows frontend, llm-service, docs,
# e2e, deploy, .git, .github or .claude, none of which they can reach.
#
# A fresh CI checkout has neither .next nor node_modules, so CI never paid this
# and nothing ever went red. It is charged entirely to the person building from
# a working tree, which after the public flip is every user who builds from
# source.
#
# Nothing excluded here is reachable from those four Dockerfiles. Their COPY
# lines name only shared/go/*, api-gateway/, backend-orchestrator/,
# backend-temporal-adapter/, shared/mcp-connectors/internal/kafka-mcp-sink/ and
# THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
#
# This file also filters the BuildKit named context `legal`, which is the repo
# root too: the images whose context is a subdirectory take THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
# from it (`COPY --from=legal`), so that file must never be excluded here.
# The list below is deliberately a DENY list rather than an allowlist: a new
# root-context Dockerfile that needs a path nobody denied keeps working, and if
# one ever does need a denied path it fails loudly at COPY, not silently.

# --- the two that dominate the context ---
frontend/
llm-service/

# --- other trees no root-context Dockerfile COPYs ---
.git/
.github/
.claude/
docs/
e2e/
deploy/
connector-deployer/
tests/
site/
examples/

# --- build and tool output, anywhere in the tree ---
**/node_modules/
**/.next/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.venv/
**/venv/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.test-evidence/
**/*.log

# --- local state that must never enter a build cache ---
.env
.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
